From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Masahiro Yamada <masahiroy@kernel.org>
Date: Sat, 10 Aug 2024 01:07:20 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] tty: vt: conmakehash: remove non-portable code printing
 comment header

The header of the generated consolemap_deftbl.c names the input font map
by the path make passes, which is absolute in an out-of-tree build, so
the build directory ends up in the generated source.

Upstream simplified the header to drop the name in v6.11, after two
earlier commits that shortened the path and that 6.6 does not have. This
is the same header change on the 6.6 base:

  /*
   * Automatically generated file; Do not edit.
   */

Upstream-Status: Backport [https://git.kernel.org/torvalds/c/7258fdd7d7459616b3fe1a603e33900584b10c13]
Signed-off-by: Masahiro Yamada <masahiroy@kernel.org>
Signed-off-by: Lee Reinhardt <l.reinhardt@peridio.com>
---
 drivers/tty/vt/conmakehash.c | 7 ++-----
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/tty/vt/conmakehash.c b/drivers/tty/vt/conmakehash.c
index cddd789..859f56b 100644
--- a/drivers/tty/vt/conmakehash.c
+++ b/drivers/tty/vt/conmakehash.c
@@ -244,16 +244,13 @@ int main(int argc, char *argv[])
 
   printf("\
 /*\n\
- * Do not edit this file; it was automatically generated by\n\
- *\n\
- * conmakehash %s > [this file]\n\
- *\n\
+ * Automatically generated file; Do not edit.\n\
  */\n\
 \n\
 #include <linux/types.h>\n\
 \n\
 u8 dfont_unicount[%d] = \n\
-{\n\t", argv[1], fontlen);
+{\n\t", fontlen);
 
   for ( i = 0 ; i < fontlen ; i++ )
     {
